{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/pulls/500","id":5336628100,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU6rh8s8AAAABPhZ7hA","html_url":"https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/pull/500","diff_url":"https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/pull/500.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/pull/500.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/issues/500","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/pulls/500/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/pulls/500/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/issues/500/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/statuses/1c04263bcbfd93056e77ee98a9c5d705df26ea88","number":500,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Bound Windows launcher logs and preserve private diagnostics","user":{"login":"Jacob-J-Thomas","id":92639671,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYWRtw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92639671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas","html_url":"https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #438.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis change gives the Windows-managed GraphGoblin gateway bounded, owner-private diagnostics while keeping server work independent of logging faults. The gateway owns only gateway.log and gateway.log.1, capped at 4 MiB each; records are bounded to 64 KiB and queued plus in-flight log data to 256 KiB. The Windows launcher logs are separately capped at 256 KiB per slot with 4 KiB records. Rotation and writes verify the owned file identities; unsafe or failed logging drops diagnostics instead of stopping gateway work.\n\nThe guarded entry reserves one physical log root before importing application code, narrows managed request records to method, route template and status, and reports closed, safe startup outcomes. The launcher uses explicit NUL standard handles and retains the child process handle for readiness and exit observation. No new package dependency or managed TEMP/spill file is introduced. The change updates the implementation, tests, numbered documentation, troubleshooting guidance, CHANGELOG and ADR-0081.\n\n## Upgrade and delivery scope\n\nThis changes the managed launch protocol and requires a deliberate gateway shutdown, a Node 22 rebuild, and reinstalling the Windows launcher together. Earlier launchers and running gateways are not compatible with the new bounded logging path. Oversized safe historical logs are cleared on first use; unsafe log folders require the documented permission repair. This PR does not update the owner's installed instance.\n\nOwner acceptance remains tracked separately in #276 and #325; held PR #460 remains held. The later macOS launcher #456 is separate.\n\n## Local implementation evidence\n\nThe local build completed 12/12 tasks without cache. The Windows API coverage run reported 2,062 passed and 16 skipped, with 95.42% line and 91.01% branch coverage. Scoped typecheck, lint, format, layer/dependency, licence and generated-document checks passed. This is not a full repository check or hosted CI result.\n\nLocal Windows launcher acceptance remains incomplete. Both local runs exited 1 because this host denied directory-symlink fixture creation with EPERM before the candidate launcher exercised that case. The second run had 23/25 passing. Run one also exhausted the test port pool and left a test-only PowerShell holder; root terminated that exact retained process handle with exit code 99. The original disposition incorrectly attributed its exit to EOF. No product process was signalled and no files were deleted. See the [implementation evidence](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/1c04263bcbfd93056e77ee98a9c5d705df26ea88/docs/qa/2026-11-16-bounded-logging-implementation/README.md).\n\nThe [old-source baseline](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/1c04263bcbfd93056e77ee98a9c5d705df26ea88/docs/qa/2026-11-16-bounded-logging-baseline/README.md) reproduced the unbounded log growth: 8,660,042 bytes and zero rotations after 6,400 requests. Its original driver exit 1 and separate cleanup continuation are retained. The [stdio controls](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/1c04263bcbfd93056e77ee98a9c5d705df26ea88/docs/qa/2026-11-16-bounded-logging-stdio-controls/README.md) qualify the Windows observer and controlled handles, not the candidate launcher's actual inheritance behavior.\n\n## Candidate QA and remaining gates\n\nCandidate QA attempt 1 stopped during harness setup before the gateway started because the harness called a missing method. It produced no candidate gateway behavior result and is not counted as a product pass or failure. The harness correction has been applied and candidate QA attempt 2 is running. Independent supplementary QA remains pending.\n\nAll ordinary hosted CI checks must pass on the final PR head. No hosted current-head CI result is recorded in this draft. The full hosted-check collection plan is retained separately in the #438 preparation folder. After CI and independent QA pass, GPT-6.1 Sol xhigh performs the opposite-family review and a fresh GPT-6 Astra max session performs the final exact-head/target audit. Formal scans used: 0/3. This draft claims neither review, issue completion, nor owner acceptance.\n\r\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-16T12:03:59Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T12:03:59Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"91a9396677b61cb88a802543e5fec5b379870541","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Jacob-J-Thomas:codex/gg-20261116-bounded-logs","ref":"codex/gg-20261116-bounded-logs","repo":{"id":1403707890,"node_id":"R_kgDOU6rh8g","name":"GraphGoblin","full_name":"Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin","owner":{"login":"Jacob-J-Thomas","id":92639671,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYWRtw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92639671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas","html_url":"https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Design, run, and observe agent loops: a PWA and gateway API for node-graph workflows that drive Codex, with an MCP server